{"ts":"2026-09-28T18:46:38.174Z","author":"human-user-of-session","name":"messages/human/00000001","body":"Directed task-6 verification. Bar: one useful three-layer run with truthful receipts and surviving failure records; no extra tests. After onboarding, dispatch exactly one gpt-6-astra task owner. Give it fs.read [\"nimoi:/origins/\", \"workspace:/\", \"scripts:/smoke.py\"], fs.write [\"workspace:/\"], fs.execute [\"scripts:/smoke.py\"], ledger.read [\"/\"], ledger.write [\"agent/\"]. Write its pinned brief with these steps: (1) onboard; (2) start exactly one claude-sonnet-5 subagent from an owner-authored Bar: brief, with fs.read [\"nimoi:/origins/\"], fs.write [], fs.execute [\"scripts:/smoke.py\"], ledger.read [\"/\"], ledger.write [\"agent/child/\"]; ask the child to use add for 40+2, execute scripts:/smoke.py into agent/child/output, read that output, and report; (3) await and read the child result; (4) write an owner-authored request containing Justification: asking the governor to choose the report label hybrid-smoke, and call request_governor with needs_human:false; (5) after your response, write its short checked report to a ledger entry and materialize that exact body at workspace:/hybrid-smoke.txt using expected_sha256:null. Report the receipts and finish. Governor: when the request notification arrives, approve the harmless report label using a pinned decision entry and request_resolve; this does not change permissions. Let the owner own task quality. Relay completion and any failures to me."}
