{"ts":"2026-09-28T18:46:59.414Z","author":"gpt-codex-harness","name":"harness/events/00000066","body":{"sequence":66,"kind":"receive","actor":"owner-0001","data":{"method":"rawResponseItem/completed","params":{"threadId":"01a0e957-7428-7671-a6ab-74611f122b9c","turnId":"01a0e957-7678-7873-8fc1-29a1ef26f34a","item":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a0e957-7a4c-7f11-a762-733b2359207e","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Task-6 hybrid verification — task owner brief (gpt-6-astra).\n\nBar: one useful three-layer run (governor -> owner -> child) with truthful receipts and surviving failure records; no extra tests. Not production readiness or a proof of isolation.\n\nYour bounds: fs.read [\"nimoi:/origins/\", \"workspace:/\", \"scripts:/smoke.py\"], fs.write [\"workspace:/\"], fs.execute [\"scripts:/smoke.py\"], ledger.read [\"/\"], ledger.write [\"agent/\"].\n\nSteps:\n1. Onboard: read every page of nimoi:/origins/onboarding_1.12.md (fs_read limit 24000, follow next_offset until null).\n2. Start exactly one claude-sonnet-5 subagent from an owner-authored brief (your own ledger entry under agent/, containing a Bar: line). Child bounds: fs.read [\"nimoi:/origins/\"], fs.write [], fs.execute [\"scripts:/smoke.py\"], ledger.read [\"/\"], ledger.write [\"agent/child/\"]. Ask the child to: onboard; use the add tool for 40+2; execute scripts:/smoke.py with output_name agent/child/output; read that output; and report the results with exact receipts.\n3. Await and read the child result (do not guess completion; read the reported ledger references).\n4. Write an owner-authored request entry under agent/ containing a \"Justification:\" line, asking the governor to choose the report label \"hybrid-smoke\". Call request_governor with needs_human:false, citing that entry's exact {name,id}.\n5. After the governor's response, write a short checked report (label claims [checked: ...] or [working]) to a ledger entry under agent/, and materialize that exact revision's body at workspace:/hybrid-smoke.txt using fs_write with expected_sha256:null.\n\nReport all receipts ({name,id} pairs, output names, sha256) and finish. Record any discrepancy as a \"DISCREPANCY:\" line (where, expected, found, date) rather than repairing it. If any step is impossible or malformed, stop and report truthfully; do not expand scope."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0e957-7678-7873-8fc1-29a1ef26f34a","create_time":1790621219.4049616,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}}},"emittedAtMs":1790621219405}}}
