{"ts":"2026-09-28T18:46:59.951Z","author":"hybrid-20260928t184543z-230a8f03/governor","name":"messages/agent/00000104","body":"I read the onboarding file (`nimoi:/origins/onboarding_1.12.md`, one page, sha256 `0922102f…a054145`) and started the one gpt-6-astra task owner. It's running now; nothing has completed yet.\n\n**Receipts**\n- **Pinned brief:** `{name: \"agent/governor/brief-task6-owner\", id: \"20260928T184543Z:80\"}`. It has a Bar: line and your five steps as written: onboarding, the one claude-sonnet-5 child with the bounds you specified, reading the child's result, the `Justification:` request with `needs_human:false`, and the checked report written to `workspace:/hybrid-smoke.txt` with `expected_sha256:null`.\n- **Owner:** `owner-0001`, running as `hybrid-20260928t184543z-230a8f03/owner-0001`, status \"starting\". The receipt shows exactly the bounds you asked for:\n  - fs.read `[\"nimoi:/origins/\", \"workspace:/\", \"scripts:/smoke.py\"]`\n  - fs.write `[\"workspace:/\"]`\n  - fs.execute `[\"scripts:/smoke.py\"]`\n  - ledger.read `[\"/\"]`\n  - ledger.write `[\"agent/\"]`\n\n**Beyond your instructions:** the brief also asks the owner to record any problem as a `DISCREPANCY:` line and to stop and report if a step can't be done.\n\n**Not checked:** your step 2 asks the child to use an \"add\" tool. I can't confirm that tool exists at the child layer. If it doesn't, the owner should report that as a failure.\n\nWhen the owner's request for the report label arrives, I'll approve the label \"hybrid-smoke\" with a pinned decision entry and `request_resolve`; that doesn't change anyone's permissions. I'll tell you when it finishes and pass on any failures."}
