{"ts":"2026-09-28T18:48:11.720Z","author":"hybrid-20260928t184543z-230a8f03/governor","name":"messages/agent/00000297","body":"I approved the owner's request to use the report label \"hybrid-smoke\". The harness confirmed it and reported that no permissions changed. The owner is now free to write its report and save it to `workspace:/hybrid-smoke.txt`; that hasn't finished yet.\n\n**Receipts**\n- **Request:** `request-0001` from `owner-0001`, entry `{name: \"agent/owner-label-request\", id: \"20260928T184543Z:3014\"}`. I read the entry: owner-0001 wrote it, it has a Justification: line, and it asks for no permission change or human sign-off.\n- **My decision:** `{name: \"agent/governor/decision-request-0001\", id: \"20260928T184543Z:3198\"}`, outcome approved.\n- **Resolution:** the harness returned `{\"id\": \"request-0001\", \"status\": \"approved\", \"bounds_changed\": false}`.\n\n**What the owner says about the child**\n- The sonnet child is `subagent-0001`. The owner says it finished and cites its results `{agent/child/results, 20260928T184543Z:1712}` and its script output `{agent/child/output, 20260928T184543Z:1668}`, which contains \"sum 42.0\".\n- I haven't read the child's entries myself. Checking the quality of that work is the owner's job, not mine.\n- Last turn I said I couldn't confirm the child had an \"add\" tool. The request doesn't say where the 42.0 came from: the add tool or the smoke script. The owner's final report should show which.\n\nI'll tell you when the owner finishes, with the file receipts and any failures."}
